[]($section.attrs('client-basic'))

Start a chat model with the [LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd')). Install the SDK in your Python environment with `python3 -m pip install openai`.

# [Send a chat message]($heading.id('send-a-chat-message'))

```=html
<div class="client-recipe">
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language icon-code">Python · client.py</span>
    <pre><code class="python" data-copy-label="Copy client.py">from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(
    base_url="http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1",
    api_key="local",
)
model_id = client.models.list().data[0].id
messages = [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello."}]

reply = client.chat.completions.create(
    model=model_id, messages=messages,
)
print(reply.choices[0].message.content)
</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="client-result">
    <figure>
      <figcaption>Example terminal output</figcaption>
      <samp>Hello!</samp>
      <code>choices[0].message.content</code>
    </figure>
    <p>Save as <code>client.py</code> and run <code>python3 client.py</code>. The greeting will vary.</p>
  </div>
</div>
```

The SDK reads the [served model ID]($link.page('llmd/reference/v1/models').ref('read-the-model-id')), including custom names. `local` is a placeholder for a local server without authentication. For a protected deployment, supply its base URL and token.

```=html
<div data-toc-parent="send-a-chat-message">
  <details class="client-disclosure" id="view-http-exchange" data-toc-label="View HTTP exchange">
    <summary>View HTTP exchange</summary>
    <p><strong>GET /v1/models</strong> returns the served model ID. This example shows the field the client reads.</p>
    <pre><code class="json">{"data": [{"id": "LFM3-1.7B-FP8"}]}</code></pre>
    <p><strong>POST /v1/chat/completions</strong> sends that same ID as <code>model</code>.</p>
    <pre><code class="json">{
  "model": "LFM3-1.7B-FP8",
  "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello."}]
}</code></pre>
    <p>The client prints <code>choices[0].message.content</code> from the reply.</p>
    <pre><code class="json">{"choices": [{"message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "Hello!"}}]}</code></pre>
  </details>
</div>
<div class="client-example-controls" role="group" aria-label="Application examples" data-pagefind-ignore hidden></div>
```

