# [Stream the reply]($heading.id('stream-a-chat-completion'))

> # [Read text as it arrives]($block.collapsible(false).attrs('client-disclosure'))
>
> Reuse `client`, `model_id`, and `messages` from the basic example. Replace the final request and print statement.
>
> ```python
> stream = client.chat.completions.create(
>     model=model_id, messages=messages, stream=True,
> )
> for chunk in stream:
>     if chunk.choices and chunk.choices[0].delta.content:
>         print(chunk.choices[0].delta.content, end="", flush=True)
> print()
> ```
>
> Each text delta extends the same line. An optional usage event has empty `choices`. The SDK stops at `[DONE]`. [Streaming HTTP example]($link.page('llmd/reference/v1/chat/completions').ref('stream-a-chat-completion'))

[]($section.attrs('client-branch'))

# [Handle a tool call]($heading.id('call-tools-from-a-client'))

> # [Execute a function and return its result]($block.collapsible(false).attrs('client-disclosure'))
>
> Use a model and chat template with tool support. Replace the lines after `model_id` in `client.py`. Your application reads its clock when LLMD asks for the time.
>
> ```python
> import json
> from datetime import datetime, timezone
>
> tools = [{"type": "function", "function": {
>     "name": "get_utc_time",
>     "description": "Read the current UTC time.",
>     "parameters": {
>         "type": "object", "properties": {}, "additionalProperties": False,
>     },
> }}]
> messages = [{"role": "user", "content": "What time is it in UTC?"}]
> reply = client.chat.completions.create(
>     model=model_id, messages=messages, tools=tools,
> )
> assistant = reply.choices[0].message
>
> if assistant.tool_calls:
>     messages.append(assistant.model_dump(exclude_none=True))
>     for call in assistant.tool_calls:
>         if call.type != "function" or call.function.name != "get_utc_time":
>             raise ValueError("Unexpected tool")
>         if json.loads(call.function.arguments) != {}:
>             raise ValueError("get_utc_time takes no arguments")
>         utc_time = datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%H:%M UTC")
>         messages.append({
>             "role": "tool",
>             "tool_call_id": call.id,
>             "content": utc_time,
>         })
>     reply = client.chat.completions.create(model=model_id, messages=messages)
>
> print(reply.choices[0].message.content)
> ```
>
> The second request includes the original assistant message and one tool result per call. Each `tool_call_id` matches the ID LLMD supplied. [Tool call fields and schema]($link.page('llmd/reference/v1/chat/completions').ref('call-tools-from-a-client'))
